<title>UK: Granada in talks to sell landmark hotel-paper.</title>
<headline>Granada in talks to sell landmark hotel-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granada Group Plc is in negotiations to sell the landmark Grosvenor House Hotel in London for more than 350 million stg, just five months after it said it was taking the property off the market, the Times said on Friday.</p>
<p>The paper, quoting company insiders, said the international hotel group, thought to be Ritz-Carlton, the U.S. luxury hotel operator controlled by Marriott International Corp, is conducting due diligence on the hotel. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
